# Design: placement-only geometry changes

## Problem
The playtest complained: nobody crosses the middle, meeting-place
distances unequal, near-gate claims unreachable. The fix had to add
no rule text - the simplification study had just paid down the rule
count.

## Approach
Treat board cells as the only free variables. Screen six placement
arms on matched seeds with the frozen gates plus three new metrics
(per-gate win rates, street-class traffic shares, per-district
exploration). Confirm finalists on 384 fresh seeds, run the parked
centered map as a diagnostic, then have three hostile reviewers
reproduce everything and attack each conclusion.

## Key Trade-offs
- Treasures must move together with posts: posts alone collapse the
  east gate (11.5%) because the faction sites stay asymmetric.
- The centered cardo map equalizes seats best but drops the first
  claimer below the predeclared floor - parked, not promoted.
- Interior gain verified not to be a farmer shuttle artifact.

